{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/855629-lfp-open-the-rogue-huntsman-changeling-2e-chronicles-using-playtestable-chunks","id":855629,"title":"[LFP, Open] The Rogue Huntsman - Changeling 2E Chronicles using Playtestable Chunks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-30T05:15:47-07:00","id":855629,"title":"[LFP, Open] The Rogue Huntsman - Changeling 2E Chronicles using Playtestable Chunks","content":"<i>The Gentry and their Huntsmen are terrifying, powerful forces wielding god-like powers that make other monsters look like drowned kittens by comparison. But despite their legendary prowess, they have rules and limitations. By understanding and exploiting them, as humans have done with beasts and other aspects of nature to survive, changelings can do the same to the True Fae and the Huntsmen to keep them at bay. The Freehold of Toronto has done just that by telling a story each night to sate the Fair Folks' hunger. It's worked well over the generations and doesn't show any signs of wavering.<br /> <br /> However, one Huntsman doesn't seem to follow the rules. In fact, it's somehow able to circumvent them, reversing them to suit its needs. It has captured several changelings of the Freehold already, and it has even gone after mortals, too. How does it defy the limitations of its very existence? No one knows. Why does it go after mortals as well as changelings? No one knows. How can one escape its Hunt?<br /> <br /> No one knows...</i> <hr />Changeling is one of my favorite gamelines, so naturally I wanted to either play/run a chronicle when the playtestable chunks came out. Since this is a seller's market and one forumite expressed interest in playing, I've decided to run.<br /> <br /> As you've probably already inferred, it's set in the Freehold of Toronto (I wanna use as much of the chunks as possible, it was also easier to use something already there than make it from scratch). At this point, I've planned a single season, a short but intense storyline. The game will be played over Skype using roll20 for rolls and atmosphere, scheduled on Thursdays at 7 PM PST (keep in mind, this isn't set in stone, the schedule can be negotiated). I've already got two players signed up, but I want at least three with a maximum of five, so there's three open slots.<br /> <br /> If you're interested, just send me a private message with your skype name and I'll send you a contact request.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> The current schedule is not on Fridays, but on Thursdays 7 PM PST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","user":"crapcarp","date":". 03-30-2016, 04:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2992-crapcarp","name":"crapcarp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}